 "response": "Realistic numeric targets to tell your doctor: fasting/premeal about 80–130 mg/dL, and 1–2 hour post‑meal under 180 mg/dL (closer to 140–160 is even better). A practical short‑term goal is to move most fasting values into the low‑130s or below and most post‑meal checks under 180 over the next 2–4 weeks — a drop of ~20–30 mg/dL in your median fasting level would be meaningful. Try to log at least 6–8 fasting readings in two weeks plus a few post‑meal checks so your clinician can see a trend. If you repeatedly see fasting >180, post‑meal >250, any single reading >300, or you develop severe symptoms (severe thirst, vomiting, confusion, etc.), call the clinic or seek urgent care right away. Keep using the 9:45 pm alarm and note whether you took your insulin so the trend reflects adherence."
