 "response": "Good move with the alarm — when you see ~200–250, first recheck in 15–30 minutes (wash/dry hands and use a fresh strip) to rule out a meter error. If it’s still high, drink water, do a light 10–20 minute walk if you feel okay, and avoid extra carbs or sugary drinks; log the value, what you ate, and whether you took your insulin. Do not double your long‑acting insulin — continue your usual schedule and call the clinic before changing any doses (follow any correction plan your clinician has already given). Call the clinic or go to urgent care if glucose stays >~300 mg/dL, you have severe symptoms (vomiting, trouble breathing, confusion, weakness), or you have moderate/large ketones. Bring these logged highs to your appointment so your clinician can decide if treatment needs adjustment."
